## Calculator
// A pocket calculator:  a number, an operator, another number, and the total as you type.
// What's where, top to bottom:
//   what it keeps:  the two numbers, the operator and the total
//   what its keys do:  clear, a digit, an operator, equals
//   how it draws:  the display, then the keypad
//   start


## What it keeps
a calculator is an app
a calculator has an input as text
a calculator has an output as text
a calculator has a left as text
a calculator has a right as text
a calculator has a total as a number
a calculator has an operator as text


## What its keys do
to clear (a calculator):
	set its input to ""
	set its output to ""
	set its left to ""
	set its operator to ""
	set its right to ""
	set its total to 0

to update the total of (a calculator):
	if its right is empty:
		set its output to ""
	otherwise
		set lhs to its left as a number
		set rhs to its right as a number
		if its operator is "+"
			set its total to lhs + rhs
		else if its operator is "–"
			set its total to lhs - rhs
		else if its operator is "×"
			set its total to lhs times rhs
		else
			set its total to lhs divided by rhs
		set its output to "= " + its total

// a digit, or the decimal point:  onto the number being typed, the left one until there's an operator
to append (digit as text) to (a calculator):
	if the digit is "."
		if its input is empty
			set its input to "0."
		otherwise if its input does not contain "."
			set its input to its input + "."
	otherwise
		set its input to its input + the digit
	if its operator is empty
		set its left to its input
	else
		set its right to its input
	update the total of the calculator

// an operator after a whole sum carries its total on, as the next sum's left number
to apply (op as text) to (a calculator):
	if its right is not empty
		finish the calculator
	set its operator to the op
	set its input to ""

// equals:  the total becomes the left number, ready for the next operator
to finish (a calculator):
	if its right is empty return
	set its left to its total as text
	set its operator to ""
	set its right to ""
	set its input to ""
	set its output to ""


## How it draws:  the display, then the keypad, four keys a row
to draw (a calculator)
	return <div class="Calculator">
		<ui-segment raised>
			<div class="Display">
				<div class="Sum">{"0" if its left is empty otherwise its left}{" "}{its operator}{" "}{its right}</div>
				<div class="Total">{its output}</div>
			</div>
			<div class="Keypad">
				<ui-button class="Wide" fluid negative onClick={clear it}>C</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid secondary onClick={finish it}>=</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid primary onClick={apply "÷" to it}>÷</ui-button>

				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "7" to it}>7</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "8" to it}>8</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "9" to it}>9</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid primary onClick={apply "×" to it}>×</ui-button>

				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "4" to it}>4</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "5" to it}>5</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "6" to it}>6</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid primary onClick={apply "–" to it}>–</ui-button>

				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "1" to it}>1</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "2" to it}>2</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "3" to it}>3</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid primary onClick={apply "+" to it}>+</ui-button>

				<ui-button class="Wide" fluid onClick={append "0" to it}>0</ui-button>
				<ui-button fluid onClick={append "." to it}>.</ui-button>
			</div>
		</ui-segment>
	</div>


## Start
set calculator to a new calculator
clear the calculator
start the calculator
